Translation patch: <VartimeRistrettoPrecomputation as VartimePrecomputedMultiscalarMul>::new (src/ristretto.rs)

Change: The lazy `static_points.into_iter().map(|P| P.borrow().0)` becomes a `Vec<EdwardsPoint>` built
by a nested helper.

Why: the Aeneas Lean library models only `Iterator::next`; the provided methods
(`map`, `zip`, `fold`, `filter`, `collect`, `rev`, `skip`, `size_hint`, `by_ref`, ...)
are missing (AeneasVerif/aeneas#1057), so the original does not build in Lean.
Aeneas also cannot extract a loop that calls `next()` directly on the `IntoIter` of a
generic `IntoIterator` parameter ("Could not find: type_var_id .. from ExtractBase.Item"),
so the consuming loop lives in a nested helper function generic over `It: Iterator`,
called with `x.into_iter()`.

Behaviour: identical. The callee immediately consumes its input completely (see below), so the
caller-visible sequence (`into_iter`, then `next()` / `borrow()` / drop per item, then drop
of the iterator) is unchanged and table construction is pure. The only difference is that
`size_hint` is no longer called on the caller's iterator. Same panics; both versions diverge
on an infinite input.

Facts relied on (not visible in the diff): `VartimePrecomputedStraus::new` (all backends) immediately does
`.into_iter().map(|P| NafLookupTable8::from(P.borrow())).collect()` and nothing else
observable.

Remove this patch when Aeneas translates the original code: delete the file,
run ./scripts/aeneas-translate.sh and `lake build`, and check both succeed.

diff --git a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
index 269662d..85d6fb5 100644
--- a/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
+++ b/curve25519-dalek/src/ristretto.rs
@@ -1010,10 +1010,22 @@ impl VartimePrecomputedMultiscalarMul for VartimeRistrettoPrecomputation {
     fn new<I>(static_points: I) -> Self
     where
         I: IntoIterator,
         I::Item: Borrow<Self::Point>,
     {
+        fn extended_points<It>(mut points: It) -> Vec<EdwardsPoint>
+        where
+            It: Iterator,
+            It::Item: Borrow<RistrettoPoint>,
+        {
+            let mut out = Vec::new();
+            while let Some(P) = points.next() {
+                out.push(P.borrow().0);
+            }
+            out
+        }
+
         Self(crate::backend::VartimePrecomputedStraus::new(
-            static_points.into_iter().map(|P| P.borrow().0),
+            extended_points(static_points.into_iter()),
         ))
     }
 
